    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "Currently, the only commands that support neovim's inccommand option are `:s` and its relatives. One feature I would _love_ to see is the `:normal` command with live changes. This would mostly eliminate the need for plugins like https://github.com/mg979/vim-visual-multi, which IMO do things differently than \"the vim way\", with inconvenient keybindings such as Alt+up/down.",
